<p>Rockaway Beach is forty minutes from Forest Hills by train. Coney Island is even closer. Every summer, New Yorkers pack their bags, grab their sunscreen, and head out without giving their eyes a second thought. Maybe they toss in a pair of drugstore sunglasses. Maybe they don&#8217;t bother at all.</p>
<p>The problem is that New York summers hit the eyes harder than most places. You have direct sun above you, UV bouncing off the water ahead, and light reflecting off the sand and pavement on both sides. The combination of all these does real damage, and most people have no idea it&#8217;s happening.</p>
